+        // HEY-CAPSULE-PACK PATCH 0008 (REMOVABLE): bound each gossip dial with a
+        // timeout. A ticket carries several candidate addrs (relay + public
+        // direct + sometimes a stale/private LAN one). endpoint.connect has NO
+        // built-in deadline, so a DEAD candidate dialed first hangs this whole
+        // sequential loop forever — wedging the provider `connect` op and Hey's
+        // awaited join_topic_with / accept-invite, even when a LATER candidate
+        // (the reachable public :4433 or the relay) would succeed. An 8s cap
+        // lets a dead candidate fail fast so the loop reaches the working one.
+        // Mirrors the timeout already used at connect_endpoint_addr.
+        // KILL CONDITION: drop when upstream bounds the gossip dial itself.
+        match tokio::time::timeout(
